@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix vag: <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness/>.
@prefix w3: <http://www.w3.org/>.
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix oa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#>.
@prefix dc11: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>.
@prefix situ: <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/situation.owl#>.
@prefix nsprov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>.

_:B29d1c3172f3abe88f52bdc40a1734c9b a owl:AllDisjointClasses;
                                    owl:members (vag:ApplicabilityContext
                                                 vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                                 vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                 vag:Dimension
                                                 vag:DimensionInContext
                                                 vag:Justification
                                                 vag:VaguenessAnnotation
                                                 vag:VaguenessType
                                                 nsprov:Agent).
_:Bad96376d84ce23678066d155b4e7bf95 a owl:AllDifferent;
                                    owl:distinctMembers (vag:qualitative-vagueness
                                                         vag:quantitative-vagueness).
_:Bdc5f1d9b085654726ebd6b0e3671db0f a owl:AllDifferent;
                                    owl:distinctMembers (vag:qualitative-vagueness
                                                         vag:quantitative-vagueness).
_:Bfb955dbc272a0dd948e777ec630854fb a owl:AllDisjointClasses;
                                    owl:members (vag:ApplicabilityContext
                                                 vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                                 vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                 vag:Dimension
                                                 vag:DimensionInContext
                                                 vag:Justification
                                                 vag:VaguenessAnnotation
                                                 vag:VaguenessType
                                                 nsprov:Agent).
dc11:creator a owl:AnnotationProperty;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy dc11:;
             rdfs:label "has creator"@en.
dc11:date a owl:AnnotationProperty;
          rdfs:isDefinedBy dc11:;
          rdfs:label "has date"@en.
dc11:description a owl:AnnotationProperty;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy dc11:;
                 rdfs:label "has description"@en.
dc11:title a owl:AnnotationProperty;
           rdfs:isDefinedBy dc11:;
           rdfs:label "has title"@en.
<http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness> dc11:creator "Panos Alexopoulos",
                                                           "Silvio Peroni";
                                              dc11:date "2013-11-28";
                                              dc11:description """Vagueness is a common human knowledge and language phenomenon, typically manifested by terms and concepts like High, Expert, Bad, Near etc.

In an OWL ontology vagueness may appear in the definitions of classes, properties, datatypes and individuals. For these entities a more explicit description of the nature and characteristics of their vagueness/non-vagueness is required.

Analyzing and describing the nature of vagueness/non-vagueness in ontological entities is subjective activity, since it is often a personal interpretation of someone (a person or, more generally, an agent).

Vagueness can be described according to at least two complementary types referring to quantitative or qualitative connotations respectively. The quantitative aspect of vagueness concerns the (real or apparent) lack of precise boundaries defining an entity along one or more specific dimensions. The qualitative aspect of vagueness concerns the identification of such other discriminants of which boundaries are not quantifiable in any precise way.

Either a vagueness description, that specifies always a type, or a non-vagueness description provides at least a justification (defined either as natural language text, an entity or a more complex logic formula, or any combination of them) that motivates a specific aspect of why an entity should be intended as vague/non-vague. Multiple justifications are possible for the same description.

The justification of a description of vagueness having quantitative type can include an explicit definition of the dimensions (defined either as natural language text, an entity or a more complex logic formula, or any combination of them) in which the entity is vague.

A description of vagueness/non-vagueness can also be context-dependent. In particular, the context-dependent objects are:

- the descriptions of vagueness/non-vagueness related to entities (i.e. the same entity can be vague in one context and non-vague in another);

- the dimensions related to a description of vagueness having quantitative type (i.e. the same entity can be vague in dimension A in one context and in dimension B in another). Note that it is the relation between a justification and a certain dimension that may specify a particular context, rather than the dimension itself.

The annotation of an entity with information about its vagueness is a particular act of tagging done by someone (i.e., an agent) who associates a description of vagueness/non-vagueness (called the body of the annotation) to the entity in consideration (called the target of the annotation)."""@en;
                                              dc11:title "The Vagueness Ontology (VO)"@en;
                                              a owl:Ontology;
                                              rdfs:comment "The Vagueness Ontology (VO) allows one to specify vagueness characterisations of the TBox entities of an ontology."@en;
                                              rdfs:label "Vagueness Ontology"@en;
                                              owl:imports <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/situation.owl>;
                                              owl:versionIRI vag:1.0;
                                              owl:versionInfo "1.0".
vag:ApplicabilityContext a owl:Class;
                         rdfs:comment "A context defines precise boundaries of application of descriptions of vagueness/non-vagueness or of the relation between a justification and a certain dimension."@en;
                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                         rdfs:label "applicability context of descriptions and related dimensions"@en.
vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness a owl:Class;
                              rdfs:comment """The descriptive characterisation of non-vagueness to associate to an ontological entity by means of an annotation. It provides at least one justification for considering the target ontological entity non-vague. This description is primarily meant to be used for entities that would typically be considered vague but which, for some reason, in the particular ontology are not. 

A description of non-vagueness is a context-dependent object, which means that it can be applied within the boundaries of a particular context (i.e. the same entity can be vague in one context and non-vague in another)."""@en;
                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                              rdfs:label "description of non-vagueness"@en;
                              rdfs:subClassOf [owl:minCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                               owl:onProperty vag:hasJustification ; 
                                               a owl:Restriction],
                                              [owl:minCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                               owl:onProperty vag:hasJustification ; 
                                               a owl:Restriction].
vag:DescriptionOfVagueness a owl:Class;
                           rdfs:comment """The descriptive characterisation of vagueness to associate to an ontological entity by means of an annotation. It specifies a vagueness type and provides at least one justification for considering the target ontological entity vague. 

A description of vagueness is a context-dependent object, which means that it can be applied within the boundaries of a particular context (i.e. the same entity can be vague in one context and non-vague in another)."""@en;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                           rdfs:label "description of vagueness"@en;
                           rdfs:subClassOf [owl:minCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasJustification ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction],
                                           [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasVaguenessType ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction],
                                           [owl:minCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasJustification ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction],
                                           [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasVaguenessType ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction].
vag:Dimension a owl:Class;
              rdfs:comment """A dimension is part of the justification of a description of quantitative vagueness. Dimensions of such a justification are used to identify what boundaries are not defined precisely by a particular entity and, thus, are part of the causes of vagueness for the entity itself. A dimension is defined either as natural language text, an entity, a more complex logic formula, or any combination of them. 

The relation between a justification and a dimension may be context-dependent, which means that it can be applied within the boundaries of a particular context (i.e. the same entity can be vague in dimension A in one context and in dimension B in another). In this case, instances of the classes 'DimensionInContext' should be used to link the justification to the related dimension."""@en;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
              rdfs:label "dimension"@en;
              rdfs:subClassOf [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasEntity ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction]
                                            [owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasLogicFormula ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction]
                                            [owl:someValuesFrom rdfs:Literal ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasNaturalLanguageText ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                               a owl:Class],
                              [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasEntity ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction]
                                            [owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasLogicFormula ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction]
                                            [owl:someValuesFrom rdfs:Literal ; 
                                            owl:onProperty vag:hasNaturalLanguageText ; 
                                            a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                               a owl:Class].
vag:DimensionInContext a owl:Class;
                       rdfs:comment "This class describes situations where a particular dimension in considered according to a particular context. In particular, instances of this class are actually specifying that the relation between a justification and a certain dimension must be considered according to a particular applicability context."@en;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                       rdfs:label "dimension in context"@en;
                       rdfs:subClassOf [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                        owl:onProperty vag:withDimension ; 
                                        a owl:Restriction],
                                       [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                        owl:onProperty vag:hasApplicabilityContext ; 
                                        a owl:Restriction],
                                       [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                        owl:onProperty vag:withDimension ; 
                                        a owl:Restriction],
                                       [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                        owl:onProperty vag:hasApplicabilityContext ; 
                                        a owl:Restriction],
                                       situ:Situation.
vag:Justification a owl:Class;
                  rdfs:comment "A justification that explains one possible reason behind a vagueness/non-vagueness description. It is defined either as natural language text, an entity, a more complex logic formula, or any combination of them."@en;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                  rdfs:label "justification for vagueness/non-vagueness description"@en;
                  rdfs:subClassOf [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                                owl:onProperty vag:hasEntity ; 
                                                a owl:Restriction]
                                                [owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                                owl:onProperty vag:hasLogicFormula ; 
                                                a owl:Restriction]
                                                [owl:someValuesFrom rdfs:Literal ; 
                                                owl:onProperty vag:hasNaturalLanguageText ; 
                                                a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                   a owl:Class],
                                  [owl:unionOf ([owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                                owl:onProperty vag:hasEntity ; 
                                                a owl:Restriction]
                                                [owl:someValuesFrom owl:Thing ; 
                                                owl:onProperty vag:hasLogicFormula ; 
                                                a owl:Restriction]
                                                [owl:someValuesFrom rdfs:Literal ; 
                                                owl:onProperty vag:hasNaturalLanguageText ; 
                                                a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                   a owl:Class].
vag:VaguenessAnnotation a owl:Class;
                        rdfs:comment "The annotation of an ontological entity with information about its vagueness is a particular act of tagging done by someone (i.e., an agent) who associates a description of vagueness/non-vagueness (called the body of the annotation) to the entity in consideration (called the target of the annotation)."@en;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                        rdfs:label "annotation of vagueness/non-vagueness"@en;
                        rdfs:subClassOf nsprov:Entity,
                                        [owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                         owl:onClass [owl:unionOf (vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                                                   vag:DescriptionOfVagueness) ; 
                                                      a owl:Class] ; 
                                         owl:onProperty oa:hasBody ; 
                                         a owl:Restriction],
                                        [owl:someValuesFrom nsprov:Agent ; 
                                         owl:onProperty nsprov:wasAttributedTo ; 
                                         a owl:Restriction],
                                        [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                         owl:onProperty oa:hasTarget ; 
                                         a owl:Restriction],
                                        [owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                         owl:onClass [owl:unionOf (vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                                                   vag:DescriptionOfVagueness) ; 
                                                      a owl:Class] ; 
                                         owl:onProperty oa:hasBody ; 
                                         a owl:Restriction],
                                        [owl:someValuesFrom nsprov:Agent ; 
                                         owl:onProperty nsprov:wasAttributedTo ; 
                                         a owl:Restriction],
                                        [owl:cardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ; 
                                         owl:onProperty oa:hasTarget ; 
                                         a owl:Restriction],
                                        oa:Annotation.
vag:VaguenessType a owl:Class;
                  rdfs:comment "A particular kind of vagueness that characterizes the entity."@en;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                  rdfs:label "vagueness type"@en.
vag:hasApplicabilityContext a owl:ObjectProperty;
                            rdfs:comment "This property links either descriptions of vagueness/non-vagueness or dimensions of descriptions of quantitative vagueness to the context to which they apply."@en;
                            rdfs:domain [owl:unionOf (vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                                      vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                      vag:DimensionInContext) ; 
                                         a owl:Class],
                                        [owl:unionOf (vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                                      vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                      vag:DimensionInContext) ; 
                                         a owl:Class];
                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                            rdfs:label "has applicability context"@en;
                            rdfs:range vag:ApplicabilityContext.
vag:hasDimension a owl:ObjectProperty;
                 rdfs:comment "It links justifications of a description of quantitative vagueness to the dimensions that identify what boundaries are not defined precisely by a particular entity and, thus, are part of the causes of vagueness for the entity itself."@en;
                 rdfs:domain [owl:intersectionOf (vag:Justification
                                                  [owl:allValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                                                         [owl:hasValue vag:quantitative-vagueness ; 
                                                                                         owl:onProperty vag:hasVaguenessType ; 
                                                                                         a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                                     a owl:Class] ; 
                                                  owl:onProperty [owl:inverseOf vag:hasJustification] ; 
                                                  a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                              a owl:Class],
                             [owl:intersectionOf (vag:Justification
                                                  [owl:allValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                                                         [owl:hasValue vag:quantitative-vagueness ; 
                                                                                         owl:onProperty vag:hasVaguenessType ; 
                                                                                         a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                                     a owl:Class] ; 
                                                  owl:onProperty [owl:inverseOf vag:hasJustification] ; 
                                                  a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                              a owl:Class];
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                 rdfs:label "has dimension"@en;
                 rdfs:range vag:Dimension;
                 owl:propertyChainAxiom (vag:hasDimensionInContext
                                         vag:withDimension),
                                        (vag:hasDimensionInContext
                                         vag:withDimension).
vag:hasDimensionInContext a owl:ObjectProperty;
                          rdfs:comment "It links justifications of a description of quantitative vagueness to situations where a particular dimension, which identifies the boundaries that are not defined precisely by a particular entity, has to be considered within a particular applicability context."@en;
                          rdfs:domain [owl:intersectionOf (vag:Justification
                                                           [owl:allValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                                                                  [owl:hasValue vag:quantitative-vagueness ; 
                                                                                                  owl:onProperty vag:hasVaguenessType ; 
                                                                                                  a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                                              a owl:Class] ; 
                                                           owl:onProperty [owl:inverseOf vag:hasJustification] ; 
                                                           a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                       a owl:Class],
                                      [owl:intersectionOf (vag:Justification
                                                           [owl:allValuesFrom [owl:intersectionOf (vag:DescriptionOfVagueness
                                                                                                  [owl:hasValue vag:quantitative-vagueness ; 
                                                                                                  owl:onProperty vag:hasVaguenessType ; 
                                                                                                  a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                                                              a owl:Class] ; 
                                                           owl:onProperty [owl:inverseOf vag:hasJustification] ; 
                                                           a owl:Restriction]) ; 
                                       a owl:Class];
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                          rdfs:label "has dimension in context"@en;
                          rdfs:range vag:DimensionInContext.
vag:hasEntity a owl:ObjectProperty;
              rdfs:comment "The entity defining the body of either a justification or dimension."@en;
              rdfs:domain [owl:unionOf (vag:Dimension
                                        vag:Justification) ; 
                           a owl:Class],
                          [owl:unionOf (vag:Dimension
                                        vag:Justification) ; 
                           a owl:Class];
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
              rdfs:label "has entity"@en.
vag:hasJustification a owl:ObjectProperty;
                     rdfs:comment "It links a particular description of vagueness/non-vagueness to a related justification."@en;
                     rdfs:domain [owl:unionOf (vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                               vag:DescriptionOfVagueness) ; 
                                  a owl:Class],
                                 [owl:unionOf (vag:DescriptionOfNonVagueness
                                               vag:DescriptionOfVagueness) ; 
                                  a owl:Class];
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                     rdfs:label "has justification"@en;
                     rdfs:range vag:Justification.
vag:hasLogicFormula a owl:ObjectProperty;
                    rdfs:comment "The logic formula defining the body of either a justification or dimension."@en;
                    rdfs:domain [owl:unionOf (vag:Dimension
                                              vag:Justification) ; 
                                 a owl:Class],
                                [owl:unionOf (vag:Dimension
                                              vag:Justification) ; 
                                 a owl:Class];
                    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                    rdfs:label "has logic formula"@en.
vag:hasNaturalLanguageText a owl:DatatypeProperty;
                           rdfs:comment "The natural language text defining the body of either a justification or dimension."@en;
                           rdfs:domain [owl:unionOf (vag:Dimension
                                                     vag:Justification) ; 
                                        a owl:Class],
                                       [owl:unionOf (vag:Dimension
                                                     vag:Justification) ; 
                                        a owl:Class];
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                           rdfs:label "has natural language text"@en;
                           rdfs:range rdfs:Literal.
vag:hasVaguenessType a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                       owl:ObjectProperty;
                     rdfs:comment "The link between a description of vagueness and the particular type of vagueness it describes."@en;
                     rdfs:domain vag:DescriptionOfVagueness;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                     rdfs:label "has vagueness type"@en;
                     rdfs:range vag:VaguenessType.
vag:isApplicabilityContextOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
                             rdfs:comment "This property links applicability contexts to the related descriptions of vagueness/non-vagueness or dimensions of descriptions of quantitative vagueness."@en;
                             rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                             rdfs:label "is applicability context of"@en;
                             owl:inverseOf vag:hasApplicabilityContext.
vag:isDimensionIn a owl:ObjectProperty;
                  rdfs:comment "It links a dimension to the situations that include related applicability contexts."@en;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                  rdfs:label "is dimension in"@en;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf situ:hasSetting;
                  owl:inverseOf vag:withDimension.
vag:isDimensionInContextOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
                           rdfs:comment "It links situations describing a dimension according to a particular context to the justification that involves them."@en;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                           rdfs:label "is dimension in context of"@en;
                           owl:inverseOf vag:hasDimensionInContext.
vag:isDimensionOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
                  rdfs:comment "It links dimensions to the justification that involves them."@en;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                  rdfs:label "is dimension of"@en;
                  owl:inverseOf vag:hasDimension.
vag:isEntityOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
               rdfs:comment "It links to the justification/dimension that involves the entity."@en;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
               rdfs:label "is entity of"@en;
               owl:inverseOf vag:hasEntity.
vag:isJustificationOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
                      rdfs:comment "It links to the description of vagueness/non-vagueness supported by the justification."@en;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                      rdfs:label "is justification of"@en;
                      owl:inverseOf vag:hasJustification.
vag:isLogicFormulaOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
                     rdfs:comment "It links to the justification/dimension that involves the logic formula."@en;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                     rdfs:label "is logic formula of"@en;
                     owl:inverseOf vag:hasLogicFormula.
vag:isVaguenessTypeOf a owl:ObjectProperty;
                      rdfs:comment "It links to the description of vagueness that has the particular vagueness type."@en;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                      rdfs:label "is vagueness type of"@en;
                      owl:inverseOf vag:hasVaguenessType.
vag:qualitative-vagueness a vag:VaguenessType,
                            owl:NamedIndividual;
                          rdfs:comment "A vagueness type that concerns the identification of such other discriminants of which boundaries are not quantifiable in any precise way."@en;
                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                          rdfs:label "qualitative vagueness"@en.
vag:quantitative-vagueness a vag:VaguenessType,
                             owl:NamedIndividual;
                           rdfs:comment "A vagueness type that concerns the (real or apparent) lack of precise boundaries defining an entity along one or more specific dimensions."@en;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                           rdfs:label "quantitative vagueness"@en.
vag:withDimension a owl:FunctionalProperty,
                    owl:ObjectProperty;
                  rdfs:comment "It links the dimension that is used in a justification according to a particular applicability context."@en;
                  rdfs:domain vag:DimensionInContext;
                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://www.essepuntato.it/2013/10/vagueness>;
                  rdfs:label "with dimension"@en;
                  rdfs:range vag:Dimension;
                  rdfs:subPropertyOf situ:isSettingFor.
oa:Annotation a owl:Class;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy oa:;
              rdfs:label "annotation"@en.
oa:hasBody dc11:description "Note that in the Annotation Ontology the intended meaning of oa:hasBody is broader than what described herein in the entity comment."@en;
           a owl:ObjectProperty;
           rdfs:comment "It links to the description of vagueness/non-vagueness involved in the annotation."@en;
           rdfs:isDefinedBy oa:;
           rdfs:label "has body"@en.
oa:hasTarget dc11:description "Note that in the Annotation Ontology the intended meaning of oa:hasTarget is broader than what described herein in the entity comment."@en;
             a owl:ObjectProperty;
             rdfs:comment "It links to the entity that has been object of the annotation."@en;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy oa:;
             rdfs:label "has target"@en.
nsprov:Agent dc11:description "Note that in the PROV Ontology the intended meaning of prov:Agent is broader than what described herein in the entity comment."@en;
             a owl:Class;
             rdfs:comment "The agent who tags an ontology entity with a vagueness/non-vagueness description."@en;
             rdfs:isDefinedBy nsprov:;
             rdfs:label "agent"@en.
nsprov:Entity a owl:Class;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy nsprov:;
              rdfs:label "entity"@en.
nsprov:wasAttributedTo dc11:description "Note that in the PROV Ontology the intended meaning of prov:wasAttributedTo is broader than what described herein in the entity comment."@en;
                       a owl:ObjectProperty;
                       rdfs:comment "It links the annotation of an ontological entity with information about its vagueness to the agent who made the annotation itself."@en;
                       rdfs:isDefinedBy nsprov:;
                       rdfs:label "was attributed to"@en.
